  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 213 AM MDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nStarting on Wednesday and through Friday, the area is expected \nto be under an upper-level ridge that amplifies towards the \nnortheast. As the ridge amplifies, a trough system to the \nsouthwest begins to move east putting us into southwesterly \nflow. With this setup, we would likely see temperatures remain \nabove seasonal, starting in the 70s and building into the 80s on\nFriday. Winds are forecast to pick up from 5-10 mph to over 20 \nmph from the south. With the upper-level southwesterly flow, \ncloud cover is also expected to build over the area as mid- to \nupper-level moisture moves through.\n\nDuring the weekend, the upper level pattern transitions into \nelongated zonal flow after the trough moves over the area \nSaturday morning. With this change in pattern, this should bring\na cold front through the area creating a chances of showers \ninto the area Saturday morning and ending Sunday morning. \nHowever with the chances of showers, it is unclear when the \nshowers could occur as forecast guidance starts to show growing \nuncertainty on timing of the trough system. If the trough speeds\nup, this would lead the cold front to pass through Friday night\nand could showers to occur all throughout Saturday. If the \ntrough slows down, we could expect the cold front to pass \nthrough Saturday afternoon and pushing the timing of showers \novernight and ending midday Sunday. Once the cold front passes \nthrough, temperatures are forecast to be back in the 70s with a \nfew lingering clouds over the area.",
